      "rev_n_1_9793be_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_9793be_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_9793be",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the midpoint K = (A + B) / 2. Since A and B are distinct integers, their sum is an integer. If the sum is even, K is an integer and the answer exists. If the sum is odd, K is a half-integer, so no integer K exists, and we print IMPOSSIBLE.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506552.0293767
      },
      "rev_n_2_155479_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_155479_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_155479",
        "thought_text": "Check the parity of (A + B). If (A + B) % 2 == 0, output (A + B) // 2. Otherwise, output IMPOSSIBLE. This avoids floating-point arithmetic entirely.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506552.0293913
      },
      "rev_n_3_08de6b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_08de6b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_08de6b",
        "thought_text": "Verify the condition |A - K| = |B - K| algebraically. Squaring both sides gives (A-K)^2 = (B-K)^2, which simplifies to A^2 - 2AK + K^2 = B^2 - 2BK + K^2, leading to 2K(A-B) = A^2 - B^2. Since A != B, K = (A+B)/2. Then check if this K is an integer.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506552.0294
      },
