        "thought_text": "Calculate the midpoint (A+B)/2. If the sum A+B is even, the midpoint is an integer and is the unique solution. If the sum is odd, the midpoint is a half-integer, so no integer K exists, output IMPOSSIBLE.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8623329782757253368",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506624.7002668
      },
      "rev_n_20_763432_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_20_763432_0",
        "node_id": "n_20_763432",
        "thought_text": "Use integer arithmetic to check parity. Compute sum = A + B. If sum % 2 == 0, print sum // 2. Otherwise, print IMPOSSIBLE. This avoids floating point issues entirely.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8623329782757253368",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506624.7002826
      },
      "rev_n_21_22819a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_21_22819a_0",
        "node_id": "n_21_22819a",
        "thought_text": "Geometrically, K must be the center of the segment connecting A and B on the number line. Since A and B are integers, the center is an integer only if the distance between them is even (i.e., A and B have the same parity).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8623329782757253368",
